00:09:55.770 --> 00:09:58.080
as a result that's causing stones to form.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:00.450
Is it safe to go in a hot tub every day?

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:02.430
I mean like I don't see the harm in it

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:04.200
as long as that hot tub is maintained and

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.660
you don't have like a
rash or any other illness,

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:08.820
just dry off after and
don't stay for too long and

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:09.653
don't overheat.

00:10:09.653 --> 00:10:10.980
Hot tubs can be problematic

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:12.180
if you have like a heart condition

00:10:12.180 --> 00:10:14.610
because they get you warmed
up and when you get warmed up,

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:17.490
your body has to kick your
heart into higher gear

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:18.900
to beat faster to cool off.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:21.690
Also, there is something
known as hot tub folliculitis

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:23.820
where you can get an infection
of your hair follicle

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:25.980
from a bacteria known as pseudomonas.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:27.780
Looks painful, feels painful sometimes.

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:29.550
Have you ever been told off by a nurse

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:30.810
for doing something dumb?

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:31.660
Absolutely.

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:34.230
Maybe not so much recently,

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:36.150
but definitely in my training days

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:37.680
I made mistakes all the time.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:38.940
In New York City when I was working

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:40.500
at a level one trauma center.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:42.600
If you mess up, they'll
shove you out of the way and

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:43.710
start doing it themselves.

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:45.900
Like when I was first learning
how to do blood draws,

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:47.010
I wasn't that great at them

00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:48.690
and I had to learn from
people who were better.

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:50.340
Most of the time they were nurses.

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:52.950
Why does swaying a baby put it to sleep?

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:55.500
It probably has something to do with

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:57.390
the movements that it's experienced when

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:59.910
the mom was moving around
and it was in utero.

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:01.740
When you have swaying,

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:04.740
you also have a constant
signal to the brain.

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:06.690
When you have a constant
signal to the brain,

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:11.070
whether it's audio, movement,
that is relaxing to us.

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:12.420
Whether we're talking about white noise

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:13.830
or we're talking about swaying a baby,

00:11:13.830 --> 00:11:15.960
I think all of that is pacifying

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:17.370
just from different variables.

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:20.190
Like one is from audio, one
is for movement, et cetera.

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:21.210
Yao Ming 2.0,

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:23.520
Dr. Mike, why does some
people have a dark neck

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:24.690
and how do you get rid of it?

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:27.180
What you might be asking
about is a condition called

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:29.571
Acanthosis nigricans which
is a darkening of your skin

00:11:29.571 --> 00:11:33.630
that can happen with
certain medical conditions,

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.730
most notably diabetes mellitus

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:38.637
where you have poor control
of your blood sugar because

00:11:38.637 --> 00:11:41.040
of a malfunction related to insulin.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:44.310
That being said, it could
be something as simple as

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:47.640
you don't wear sunblock and
you're exposed to sunlight

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:49.140
on the back of your
neck and not the front.

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:51.210
So like it really is important that

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:52.830
you do a thorough history and physical

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:54.660
before you just go start ordering tests.

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:56.340
What are your thoughts
on medical professionals

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:58.890
using their place of work to
make a social media content?

00:11:58.890 --> 00:12:00.360
Would you as a patient feel comfortable

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:02.550
visiting a doctor who
was on social media and

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:04.740
used a practice you were
visiting as their studio,

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:05.573
so to speak?

00:12:05.573 --> 00:12:07.410
Well, it depends on how they're using it.

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:09.510
Are they using it respectfully to educate

00:12:09.510 --> 00:12:11.490
without making anyone feel uncomfortable

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:13.680
and still respecting everyone's privacy?

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:14.670
If so, why not?

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:15.930
I would be excited to go there.

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:19.650
Because I know what that doctor
or that practice stands for.

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:22.080
I actually get kind of an
inside look on how they work

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:25.170
and it gives me insight
into their relationships

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:27.750
and if I know that they're
all close with the staff,

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:29.430
that kind of makes me feel at ease.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:31.230
What are some alternatives to therapy?

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:32.100
It's not for everyone.

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:33.840
There has to be other options, right?

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:36.360
Well, first of all, there are
different types of therapy.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:38.730
Family therapy, DBT, CBT,

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:40.440
but really the ultimate thing that decides

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:43.710
success in therapy is your
connection to your therapist.

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:47.250
There's all types of other
therapies, equine therapy,

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:49.410
animal therapy, music therapy

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:51.900
that can be used in specific situations,

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:54.120
but it's always important
to make that decision

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:56.340
with the help of a mental
health professional

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:57.480
or a medical doctor.

00:12:57.480 --> 00:13:00.420
Should I wear gloves when I lift weights?

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.430
You can go in many
directions here, Bailey.

00:13:02.430 --> 00:13:04.550
Some people for aesthetic reasons

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:06.270
will choose to wear gloves.

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:08.070
They wanna prevent calluses from forming.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:10.200
I think the callus is beneficial

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:12.060
as long as it's a healthy callus,

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:14.820
meaning that it's not too
big, it's not overly dry.

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:16.080
Because what happens is if it gets

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:19.800
really big and overly dry,
it can totally rip off

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:21.900
and then you have no padding
at all for the weight.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.820
So you need to be smart
and in some instances

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:26.970
maybe wear gloves or even
they have some of these grips

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:29.310
where you can just like put on a grip and

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:30.480
you don't have a full glove,

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:32.820
therefore you're not like
retaining all that moisture

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:35.280
on your whole hand, but
only on the palm or surface.

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:37.380
What's a nice gift to
give a doctor or nurses

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:39.930
or other hospital staff
after an extended stay?

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:42.780
I think the rule is
medically, ethically speaking,

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:45.240
it has to be under $30 or something.

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:46.590
That's the the guideline set

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:47.940
by a professional organizations.

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:50.760
Making a nice meal for
them, some cookies or

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:53.280
an inexpensive bottle of wine
if you know they like wine.

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:55.290
If you're my patient,
don't get me anything.

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:58.710
Just stay happy and healthy
and keep working on yourself.

